spread":0.035992420388192045,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":18.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.42199251022978806,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":29.7,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.16731118976161052,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":89.1,"_gate_pool_share":0.10661829053479321,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":82.6,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.04782085172873507,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":48.9,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.02049233266088903,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":20.5,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03123746016994779,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":45.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.022748605169374825,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":78.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0048255163891013945,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":92.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.0025099998,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.091,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":9.1,"pf":[],"description_full":"Linde plc operates as an industrial gas company worldwide. The company offers atmospheric gases, including oxygen, nitrogen, argon, and rare gases; and process gases, such as hydrogen, helium, carbon dioxide, carbon monoxide, electronic gases, specialty gases, and acetylene. It also engages in the design and construction of turnkey process plants for third-party customers, as well as for its gas businesses, including air separation, hydrogen, synthesis, olefin, and natural gas plants. The company serves the healthcare, chemicals and energy, manufacturing, metals and mining, food and beverage, and electronics industries. It operates in the United States, Brazil, Mexico, Canada, Germany, the United Kingdom, Eastern Europe, China, Australia, South Korea, and India. Linde plc was founded in 1879 and is based in Woking, the United Kingdom.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sanjiv  Lamba | CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 61 | Compensation: $5.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 64K people. Revenue per employee of $527K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers, improving at 13%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $79K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Linde plc is a mega-cap basic materials business with a $236.5B market cap on $34.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 8% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $5.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.50\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 35\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 215% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.153347602593499},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.3pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (91% sell ratio, net $57.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Basic Materials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 17% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","33 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Did Linde (NASDAQ:LIN) Reveal in Its Record Quarter? - Kalkine Media","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/bluechip/what-did-linde-nasdaqlin-reveal-in-its-record-quarter","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793814900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"56,7