% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 6% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 19% and a beta of 0.62, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.10 vs 5y 0.58), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $940.3M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 33% in the 2020 crash, 23% in the 2022 bear market and 52% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $163 (margin of safety -215%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 6%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $122 to $222 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks expensive against Basic Materials peers: P/E 34.2 vs 16.5, EV/EBITDA 19.1 vs 8.5 and P/FCF 46.5 vs 22.8 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 9% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 2.2% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 3.4% (vs the 8% bar).","The 27 covering analysts target $551 on average, 7% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 12% earns above the cost of capital of 8.0%, but the 4pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.42).","It converts 15% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality is mixed: cash conversion of 1.50x, but a weak Piotroski score of 3/9.","ROE of 18% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.3x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 5pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.5% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.7x net debt to EBITDA ($5.1B of cash against $27.0B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 35.0x.","The current ratio of 0.88 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.6% over 3 years and 4.5% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 31%).","At current returns, reinvesting 18% of profits supports about 2.0% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 4.8% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are contracting (-1.3% trend).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.12 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 1.8x annual revenue and deferred revenue up 10%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.4x, 15.5% of sales), a maintenance pace."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and institutions hold 89%.","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 10 sales over the past year, net $57.9M sold.","It returns 3.1% a year to shareholders (1.9% in buybacks and 1.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 2.3% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 33 consecutive years, raising it 6.7% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 64,512 employees, each generates about $527K of revenue, 0.8x the Basic Materials median, and productivity has risen 12.5% a year.","That works out to $79K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $5.0M (9x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":44,"head":"Avoid: priced 215% above its fair value of $163.","pros":["FCF margin 15.0%","Altman Z in the safe zone","12-1 month momentum +20%","Returns 3.1% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 215% above fair value of $163","Piotroski F-score 3/9","P/E 34.2x vs sector 16.5x","EV/EBITDA 19.1x vs sector 8.5x","P/FCF 46.5x vs sector 22.8x"],"flags":["Priced 215% above its fair value of $163"],"need":[],"buy_below":138.89,"vc":{"base":163.4,"base_src":"dcf","bear":122.38,"bull":222.01,"alt_median":150.66,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.1208,"dispersion":0.057,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":16.4623,"ev_ebitda":8.463,"pfcf":22.7638,"pb":2.1738,"roic":0.0591,"gross_margin":0.256,"fcf_margin":0.052,"div_yield":0.0194}},"ticker":"LIN","date":"2026-11-06"}